{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFMCKajGncZWBwE9tK36","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ruled F1 **FIX**: the finding is real. The verdict is committed as `3d7e66e73` in `docs/reviews/wi-963/007-ADJUDICATE-1ae50f4.md`, with both required trailers.\n\n**The reproduction.** I ran the finding's sequence in a scratch test outside the repo, using the lane's own test helpers and the real snapshot producer:\n1. Amend SR-001, then act A re-attests SR-001.\n2. Re-point SR-001's `SN-Refs` and amend SR-002.\n3. Act B re-attests only SR-002.\n\nBoth rows are recorded as amended, but the mint files nothing for either. Act B copies the whole registry, and a traced cell doesn't count as drift, so the copy took the re-point without anyone ruling on it. The filter then sees SR-001 as re-attested in the range (by act A) and equal to the copy at `after` (written by act B), and treats it as settled.\n\n**Why FIX:**\n- **It breaks the Done-when:** \"re-attested … then amended again after its act still yields its amendment row.\" This mint counts a routed traced cell as an amendment, and the lane's own test pins that a re-point after the act must still mint.\n- **The kit's own route reaches it, with no hand edits.** Lanes hold more than one checkpoint, and a later act on the same registry copies it whole. The amendment brief selects rows only by drift in approved cells, so the second checkpoint never shows SR-001 and its act leaves SR-001 out.\n- **The change becomes silent.** Before the filter, the trunk mint at least filed a visible row for the re-point. Now nothing records it.\n- **Not ESCALATE or SUCCESSOR.** A Done-when gap can't be SUCCESSOR, and the fix is local to the filter's own condition, so it isn't an owner-level risk.\n\n**The fix the ruling asks for:**\n- Compare the row against the copy the re-attesting act itself wrote, at the commit that added that ledger entry, rather than the copy at `after`.\n- Amend LLR-342 and TC-373 to match, add a regression with two acts on one registry and a routed traced edit between them, and re-sit the amended rows.\n\nAs in the earlier commits, the hook's `format` step was skipped (no ruff for its Python 3.12). I left the coordinator's `.requested` marker untracked."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4829,"cache_read_input_tokens":261781,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4829},"output_tokens":743,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f031c6a5-ecf0-490f-9890-c7a8a87f92fc","uuid":"5d0e6d0f-f393-405b-a51a-f593858e921e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T12:03:48.195Z","request_id":"req_011CgFMCJmcSbypk6Z9AtCkB"}
